## 1. Scope
- No requirements extracted due to missing description.
- Constraints: Jira access unauthorized. Description field missing.
- In Scope:
  - Jira API authentication validation
  - Error handling for missing description
- Out of Scope:
  - Functional testing of AD-488 requirements (not possible without description)

## 2. Test Approach
- Testing Levels:
  - API / Service Integration Level (Jira authentication and issue retrieval endpoint validation)
  - Error Handling / Application Response Validation Level (Unauthorized and missing-description response paths)
  - End-to-End Integration Level (Client request through Jira API access failure handling flow)
- Testing Types:
  - Functional Integration Testing
  - Negative Testing
  - Error Handling and Resilience Validation
  - Regression Testing (limited to authentication and retrieval failure handling paths)
- Test Design Techniques:
  - Equivalence Partitioning (valid credentials vs invalid credentials vs insufficient permissions)
  - State Transition Testing (authorized to unauthorized access states and resulting system behavior)
  - Decision Table Testing (response handling based on authentication status and description availability)
  - Negative Testing (401 Unauthorized and inaccessible description scenarios)
- Environments Needed:
  - Integration or staging environment with controlled Jira API connectivity
  - Test accounts matrix covering valid access, invalid token, and insufficient-permission roles
  - Mock or stub Jira API service capable of returning 401 Unauthorized and empty/missing description responses
  - Centralized logging/monitoring access to verify error propagation and handling behavior
- Approach Description: The execution strategy is limited strictly to the approved scope because no business requirement content is available from the Jira issue description. Testing will focus on validating Jira API authentication behavior, permission-based access outcomes, and the consuming system's handling of 401 Unauthorized or missing-description conditions. API-level tests will verify retrieval behavior across credential and permission partitions, while negative tests will confirm that inaccessible issue descriptions are surfaced as controlled errors without downstream failures. End-to-end integration checks will validate that the client workflow pauses cleanly at Human-in-the-Loop Gate 2 when architectural input cannot be derived from the source issue content. No feature-level functional validation for AD-488 business requirements will be designed or executed because that area is explicitly out of scope.

## 3. Quality Objectives
- Validate Jira API authentication and access permissions.
- Verify error handling for missing or inaccessible issue descriptions.

