## 6. Test Schedule / Milestone
- Test design: 2 days
- Environment setup: 1 day
- Script development: 2 days
- Execution: 2 days
- Reporting: 1 day
- Total duration: 8 days
- Resources: 1 QA automation engineer, 1 test lead

## 7. Assumptions
- Test accounts and mock Jira API endpoints will be available.
- Centralized logging is enabled.
- No business requirements are available for functional validation.

## 9. Risk Mitigation Table
Risk ID | Description | Severity | Likelihood | Mitigation Action
---|---|---|---|---
R1 | Dynamic database sheet connection drops during API auth | High | Medium | Use tcconfig to simulate and PyTest to validate recovery/retry logic
R2 | SLA processing latency in Jira API | Medium | Medium | Use JMeter to simulate load and validate timeout handling
R3 | Unauthorized access due to expired/invalid tokens | High | High | Automate negative tests with PyTest and OWASP ZAP; alert on repeated failures
R4 | Incomplete error logging/monitoring | Medium | Medium | Ensure centralized logging is enabled and validated in all test runs
R5 | Test environment instability (mock API outages) | Medium | Medium | Use tcconfig to simulate outages and validate system resilience
